1
00:00:25,253 --> 00:00:26,699
It’s okay. I just had a fight.

2
00:00:26,976 --> 00:00:28,269
With your dad again?

3
00:00:28,269 --> 00:00:29,478
I really need to leave.

4
00:00:31,681 --> 00:00:32,932
I understand.

5
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:37,471
Being vulnerable sometimes is scary.

6
00:00:38,756 --> 00:00:42,427
But not being able to open up
doesn’t make you a bad person.

7
00:00:43,714 --> 00:00:46,133
Are you asking me out again?

8
00:00:46,508 --> 00:00:48,385
Yes. A date.

9
00:00:48,385 --> 00:00:50,137
Then you’ll just ditch me again.

10
00:00:51,388 --> 00:00:53,640
I guess we’re both inside
the waiting room, huh?

11
00:00:53,665 --> 00:00:54,682
Willing to wait.

12
00:00:56,351 --> 00:00:58,145
Willing to wait for her, too.

13
00:01:00,522 --> 00:01:02,816
Just wanted to ask if you’re free today?

14
00:01:03,059 --> 00:01:04,853
Or let me know when you’re available.

15
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:08,061
Hi, I’m free at 6 today.

16
00:01:09,753 --> 00:01:13,423
Okay. I’ll pick you up at 6! See you!

17
00:01:14,174 --> 00:01:16,844
Okay. Everything’s gonna be okay, Ke.
Everything’s gonna be okay.

18
00:01:17,177 --> 00:01:19,680
It’s okay. I’m here,
you're safe.

19
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,431
Calm down. It's okay.

20
00:03:04,409 --> 00:03:07,871
Are you on your way?
Don’t arrive too soon.

21
00:03:07,871 --> 00:03:13,252
I’m still getting ready.

22
00:03:13,252 --> 00:03:15,837
I’m on my way.
There’s no rush.

23
00:03:15,837 --> 00:03:18,215
Take your time.

24
00:03:53,750 --> 00:03:54,793
Hi, Kierra.

25
00:03:55,419 --> 00:03:56,795
Hi, have you been waiting long?

26
00:03:57,462 --> 00:03:58,964
No, I just got here.

27
00:03:59,339 --> 00:04:00,299
Where are we going?

28
00:04:00,882 --> 00:04:02,342
I prepared a few things to do tonight,

29
00:04:02,342 --> 00:04:04,636
but if you have something in mind,
we can do that instead.

30
00:04:04,636 --> 00:04:06,054
No, let’s do your plan.

31
00:04:12,978 --> 00:04:14,313
Do you want anything?

32
00:04:16,064 --> 00:04:19,318
But if you want my suggestion,
this one is really good—

33
00:04:20,402 --> 00:04:21,486
their Kare-kare.

34
00:04:22,237 --> 00:04:23,447
Okay, I’ll have that, then.

35
00:04:23,447 --> 00:04:24,323
Okay.

36
00:04:24,656 --> 00:04:26,616
But if you want anything else,
just place your order, okay?

37
00:04:34,958 --> 00:04:36,126
Can I ask you something?

38
00:04:36,501 --> 00:04:37,336
Hm?

39
00:04:37,887 --> 00:04:39,931
But if you’re not comfortable, it’s okay.

40
00:04:41,882 --> 00:04:43,175
It’s something personal.

41
00:04:46,386 --> 00:04:48,263
Are you still having nightmares?

42
00:04:51,099 --> 00:04:54,269
I didn’t have any last night.

43
00:04:55,103 --> 00:04:59,983
The other day, however, I did.
And the days before that, too.

44
00:05:02,611 --> 00:05:07,491
I’d rather you don’t
ask me about that anymore.

45
00:05:11,036 --> 00:05:12,662
What about you?

46
00:05:13,288 --> 00:05:15,499
What happened?
Why did you ditch me last time?

47
00:05:20,170 --> 00:05:21,713
My dad and I had a fight.

48
00:05:24,282 --> 00:05:25,408
We’re not okay.

49
00:05:27,761 --> 00:05:30,889
Actually, I saw you that time.

50
00:05:31,848 --> 00:05:35,227
You were with a girl,
so I didn’t bother you.

51
00:05:37,062 --> 00:05:38,021
A girl?

52
00:05:38,021 --> 00:05:38,772
Yeah.

53
00:05:39,356 --> 00:05:41,024
You were even hugging.

54
00:05:42,776 --> 00:05:43,610
Shan!

55
00:05:46,279 --> 00:05:47,239
Oh!

56
00:05:47,614 --> 00:05:48,907
Ah, Helen.

57
00:05:49,825 --> 00:05:51,118
She’s a close friend of mine.

58
00:05:51,785 --> 00:05:55,080
She came to see me because she found
out about what happened to my father.

59
00:05:55,747 --> 00:05:57,833
So she just went there
to check up on me.

60
00:05:59,084 --> 00:06:00,127
Okay, then.

61
00:06:04,005 --> 00:06:07,259
So, are you angry with me because
you saw me hugging someone else?

62
00:06:07,426 --> 00:06:10,345
Because you didn’t show up.
Don’t put words in my mouth.

63
00:06:11,513 --> 00:06:13,682
Let’s just order.
You’re pissing me off.

64
00:06:16,143 --> 00:06:19,396
You’d better be careful. Because
I might think you’re getting jealous.

65
00:06:19,771 --> 00:06:20,939
As if.

66
00:06:22,566 --> 00:06:27,737
Don't worry. I'm all yours right now.
I'll make it up to you.

67
00:06:37,372 --> 00:06:38,415
Excuse me.

68
00:06:39,875 --> 00:06:41,209
Why did you go to law school?

69
00:06:42,345 --> 00:06:43,346
It’s challenging.

70
00:06:45,057 --> 00:06:47,393
Why did you get into
the coffee shop business?

71
00:06:48,091 --> 00:06:49,676
It’s also challenging.

72
00:06:51,958 --> 00:06:54,460
If only making decisions were that easy.

73
00:06:54,714 --> 00:06:56,716
Your reasoning is very simple.

74
00:06:57,184 --> 00:06:59,144
Or maybe I just don’t want to elaborate.

75
00:06:59,691 --> 00:07:01,873
Because if I start
telling you about it, you

76
00:07:01,897 --> 00:07:04,029
might end up hearing
my whole life story.

77
00:07:05,734 --> 00:07:08,236
And don’t you want to share
the story of your life?

78
00:07:12,032 --> 00:07:15,327
Do you want to share your whole life story?

79
00:07:18,538 --> 00:07:20,624
I don’t think I’m ready.

80
00:07:20,999 --> 00:07:23,460
It’s fine. You don’t
have to tell me anything.

81
00:07:35,847 --> 00:07:36,806
It’s nice.

82
00:07:36,806 --> 00:07:39,226
Why do you know so much about clothes?

83
00:07:39,601 --> 00:07:40,685
Oh…

84
00:07:41,269 --> 00:07:42,979
Because my sister loves to shop.

85
00:07:43,188 --> 00:07:44,630
She loves going
clothes shopping— to the

86
00:07:44,654 --> 00:07:46,358
point where I end up
carrying all her things.

87
00:07:46,358 --> 00:07:49,110
She makes me carry her bags
every time she goes shopping.

88
00:07:49,486 --> 00:07:50,028
Ah.

89
00:07:50,028 --> 00:07:51,947
No, no, it’s okay.

90
00:07:51,947 --> 00:07:53,240
Are you talking about Elyse?

91
00:07:54,199 --> 00:07:54,908
What?

92
00:07:55,242 --> 00:07:56,618
How’d you know my sister?

93
00:07:58,578 --> 00:08:02,082
She is a friend of my friend.
I see her a lot at our school.

94
00:08:02,666 --> 00:08:04,918
At your school? Really?

95
00:08:05,835 --> 00:08:07,128
How does she get there?

96
00:08:07,457 --> 00:08:11,419
Oh... maybe she just looks like her.

97
00:08:11,466 --> 00:08:13,168
Yeah, maybe she just looks like her.

98
00:08:14,427 --> 00:08:15,679
Just a look-alike.

99
00:08:19,015 --> 00:08:19,182
Oh, right—

100
00:08:19,182 --> 00:08:20,350
Oh, right—

101
00:08:22,602 --> 00:08:23,770
Can you go over there?

102
00:08:23,770 --> 00:08:24,938
Go over there. Just go.

103
00:08:24,938 --> 00:08:25,772
- Just go.
- - Why—

104
00:08:25,772 --> 00:08:27,774
- Just go.
- Why—

105
00:08:27,774 --> 00:08:30,569
I... I have to buy something.

106
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:34,097
Yeah. I need to buy some underwear.

107
00:08:35,699 --> 00:08:37,701
Okay? Stay there, okay. Just stay there.

108
00:08:47,335 --> 00:08:48,336
Shan?

109
00:08:49,337 --> 00:08:50,297
Elyse?

110
00:08:57,429 --> 00:08:58,430
Hey, Ke. What’s up?

111
00:08:58,767 --> 00:08:59,851
Where are you?

112
00:09:00,430 --> 00:09:04,017
At the mall. Why? What about you?
Did something happen? Are you okay?

113
00:09:04,144 --> 00:09:05,520
Oh, okay.

114
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:08,548
Yes, I’m fine.
I just had something to ask you.

115
00:09:08,732 --> 00:09:09,649
What is it?

116
00:09:09,941 --> 00:09:13,477
Don’t move, just stay where you are.

117
00:09:13,502 --> 00:09:15,754
Huh? What are you talking about?

118
00:09:16,656 --> 00:09:20,535
I mean, suddenly I’ve got
a craving for kwek-kwek—yeah.

119
00:09:21,202 --> 00:09:22,245
Is there any in the mall?

120
00:09:22,245 --> 00:09:23,496
How should I know?

121
00:09:23,997 --> 00:09:27,751
Why don’t you look for some
on the street or order home delivery?

122
00:09:28,293 --> 00:09:33,173
Eh, never mind—I’m not hungry anymore.
Yeah, Sevi. Yeah. I’m fine now.

123
00:09:33,173 --> 00:09:35,258
Okay, take care, okay. Enjoy your date.

124
00:09:35,258 --> 00:09:35,884
Bye.

125
00:09:35,884 --> 00:09:37,135
Huh? What date?

126
00:09:40,221 --> 00:09:44,100
Don't worry, Sevi.
I'll keep this secret. Good luck.

127
00:09:44,424 --> 00:09:45,050
Ke.

128
00:09:47,836 --> 00:09:49,170
Are you hiding from me?

129
00:09:49,195 --> 00:09:51,364
No. I’m just on the phone with someone.

130
00:09:51,927 --> 00:09:53,720
I thought you were buying your undies?

131
00:09:53,793 --> 00:09:55,503
Huh? Undies?

132
00:09:55,609 --> 00:09:56,527
Undies.

133
00:09:56,694 --> 00:09:58,696
Sun... Sunnies. I said sunnies.

134
00:09:58,721 --> 00:10:00,348
You said underwear.

135
00:10:00,450 --> 00:10:03,286
I don’t need your opinion on that subject,
thank you very much.

136
00:10:03,286 --> 00:10:05,163
Let me help you pick.
Come on, let’s choose together.

137
00:10:05,163 --> 00:10:05,747
No need.

138
00:10:06,081 --> 00:10:06,748
Let’s go.

139
00:10:06,905 --> 00:10:07,781
So, where to next?

140
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:08,917
Froyo?

141
00:10:08,917 --> 00:10:09,793
Okay, let’s go.

142
00:10:10,126 --> 00:10:11,002
Not the underwear?

143
00:10:11,002 --> 00:10:11,815
Yes.

144
00:10:13,672 --> 00:10:14,589
So how was it?

145
00:10:17,342 --> 00:10:18,134
The date?

146
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,763
It’s okay.

147
00:10:22,235 --> 00:10:23,402
I had fun.

148
00:10:24,974 --> 00:10:28,728
The truth is, I don’t know what
the definition of a perfect date is.

149
00:10:29,688 --> 00:10:31,356
I don’t really go on dates much.

150
00:10:33,233 --> 00:10:34,156
What do you mean?

151
00:10:34,639 --> 00:10:36,265
You didn’t go on dates with your ex?

152
00:10:42,367 --> 00:10:45,954
Our dates weren’t dates.

153
00:10:48,123 --> 00:10:49,332
They were...

154
00:10:50,625 --> 00:10:52,168
They were nightmares.

155
00:10:56,631 --> 00:10:57,590
I’m sorry.

156
00:10:59,342 --> 00:11:00,385
Got something in my eye.

157
00:11:05,974 --> 00:11:07,475
Do you like reading books?

158
00:11:09,102 --> 00:11:09,936
A bit.

159
00:11:10,734 --> 00:11:12,235
Do you want to come
with me to the bookstore?

160
00:11:12,888 --> 00:11:16,433
I have some books to buy.
You can buy some too—it’s on me.

161
00:11:17,068 --> 00:11:18,236
I won’t turn that down.

162
00:11:18,805 --> 00:11:19,681
- Let’s go.
- Let’s go then.

163
00:11:21,781 --> 00:11:22,574
Give me that—

164
00:11:22,574 --> 00:11:23,867
No it’s okay. I got it.

165
00:11:27,078 --> 00:11:27,912
Sure?

166
00:11:32,834 --> 00:11:33,710
Do you like your book?

167
00:11:34,294 --> 00:11:36,171
Yeah, I do. I got two.

168
00:11:37,005 --> 00:11:38,548
What are they about?

169
00:11:39,048 --> 00:11:43,762
One is about architecture,
and the other is a romantic comedy.

170
00:11:44,387 --> 00:11:45,096
Nice.

171
00:11:45,096 --> 00:11:45,722
Yeah.

172
00:11:46,848 --> 00:11:47,807
- Here—
- Sorry, Ke.

173
00:11:48,725 --> 00:11:51,186
I’m going to the bathroom.
I’ll be quick. I’ll be right back.

174
00:11:51,186 --> 00:11:51,787
Okay.

175
00:11:52,145 --> 00:11:52,896
Wait for me.

176
00:11:52,896 --> 00:11:53,605
Okay.

177
00:11:56,399 --> 00:11:58,318
Hey! Shan!

178
00:11:58,568 --> 00:11:59,694
Miguel.

179
00:12:00,904 --> 00:12:02,280
Nice seeing you here.

180
00:12:02,781 --> 00:12:05,074
Look at you.
Dressed to impress, huh?

181
00:12:05,241 --> 00:12:06,701
Hot stuff!

182
00:12:07,827 --> 00:12:08,495
Who’s with you?

183
00:12:08,495 --> 00:12:09,245
Who are you with?

184
00:12:09,949 --> 00:12:10,658
You have a girl?

185
00:12:12,332 --> 00:12:13,208
Girlfriend?

186
00:12:14,667 --> 00:12:16,920
I thought we were playing around.
I thought we were the same.

187
00:12:18,421 --> 00:12:20,173
I had no idea you liked to gossip.

188
00:12:20,590 --> 00:12:22,383
I think you should mind your own business.

189
00:12:26,759 --> 00:12:30,096
I think you should
introduce me to your new girl.

190
00:12:32,185 --> 00:12:33,937
And I think she just left you.

191
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:02,423
Ke?

192
00:13:07,178 --> 00:13:07,637
Ke?

193
00:13:08,096 --> 00:13:09,389
Ke, it’s okay.

194
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:10,807
It’s okay.

195
00:13:10,807 --> 00:13:12,809
It’s okay.

196
00:13:13,852 --> 00:13:15,937
It’s okay. I’m here, you're safe.

197
00:13:16,229 --> 00:13:17,730
Calm down. It's okay.

198
00:13:19,858 --> 00:13:21,025
You're safe.

199
00:13:22,235 --> 00:13:23,194
Let’s go?

200
00:13:26,614 --> 00:13:27,574
Let’s go?

201
00:13:29,242 --> 00:13:30,201
It's okay.

202
00:13:57,130 --> 00:13:58,923
Hi, Shan. This is Sam.

203
00:13:59,772 --> 00:14:02,567
Hey, Sam. How is she?

204
00:14:03,818 --> 00:14:05,278
She’s sleeping now.

205
00:14:05,434 --> 00:14:08,103
Shan, were you with her earlier?

206
00:14:09,115 --> 00:14:10,491
Yeah, we’re…

207
00:14:11,117 --> 00:14:12,493
We were actually on a date.

208
00:14:12,911 --> 00:14:16,623
Ah, I see. I’m sorry.
We’ve already taken her home.

209
00:14:17,636 --> 00:14:20,055
She’s not in a good state.
I hope you understand.

210
00:14:21,294 --> 00:14:24,047
Yeah. I understand.

211
00:14:24,703 --> 00:14:27,206
Thank you. Please take care of her.

212
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:30,218
I’ll tell Ke to call you
when things are okay.

213
00:14:31,554 --> 00:14:32,555
Yes, please.

214
00:14:33,056 --> 00:14:33,973
Thank you.

215
00:15:02,139 --> 00:15:02,973
Bro.

216
00:15:03,007 --> 00:15:03,821
Hey.

217
00:15:04,462 --> 00:15:06,339
What’s up? Sorry, I’m late.

218
00:15:06,339 --> 00:15:07,507
Have a seat.

219
00:15:07,507 --> 00:15:08,466
Thanks, bro.

220
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:10,176
This one’s mine?

221
00:15:10,677 --> 00:15:11,469
Okay.

222
00:15:13,522 --> 00:15:14,315
Lopez?

223
00:15:14,973 --> 00:15:17,433
Oh fuck, it’s Shan!

224
00:15:17,433 --> 00:15:18,685
This must be fate.

225
00:15:18,685 --> 00:15:20,019
We meet again.

226
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:21,754
‘Sup?

227
00:15:22,628 --> 00:15:25,047
Who is the girl you
were talking to earlier?

228
00:15:28,694 --> 00:15:30,655
I’m talking to you;
why don’t you talk to me?

229
00:15:31,254 --> 00:15:31,838
Hey.

230
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,910
Talk to me first,
and then you can get it back.

231
00:15:37,954 --> 00:15:39,747
It’s yours. I don’t care about that.

232
00:15:42,709 --> 00:15:43,793
Damn. What a bore.

233
00:15:50,633 --> 00:15:52,468
He doesn’t want to talk.
He’s being dramatic.

234
00:15:53,386 --> 00:15:55,555
Hey! Shan!

235
00:15:56,014 --> 00:15:57,974
You should introduce me to your new girl.

236
00:15:59,183 --> 00:16:01,019
And I think she just left you.

237
00:16:13,114 --> 00:16:14,657
I don’t really go on dates much.

238
00:16:15,366 --> 00:16:16,993
You didn’t go on dates with your ex?

239
00:16:17,361 --> 00:16:20,948
Our dates weren’t dates.

240
00:16:21,167 --> 00:16:22,210
They were…

241
00:16:22,957 --> 00:16:24,375
They were nightmares.

242
00:16:24,751 --> 00:16:26,794
Stop, stop…

243
00:16:26,794 --> 00:16:27,837
Stop…

244
00:16:27,837 --> 00:16:29,172
Enough!

245
00:16:29,714 --> 00:16:30,506
Kierra?

246
00:16:30,506 --> 00:16:31,758
Kierra, Kierra.

247
00:16:31,758 --> 00:16:33,009
Hey, hey, you're okay.

248
00:16:33,217 --> 00:16:33,885
Who is it?

249
00:16:34,135 --> 00:16:36,095
The person you see in your dreams.

250
00:16:38,598 --> 00:16:39,557
My ex.

251
00:17:16,010 --> 00:17:18,221
Ke? Are you okay?

252
00:17:21,808 --> 00:17:24,185
Rest for now.
Don’t push yourself too hard.

253
00:17:29,273 --> 00:17:30,274
Hey.

254
00:17:32,610 --> 00:17:33,694
Sam…

255
00:17:34,946 --> 00:17:36,447
It’s so frustrating.

256
00:17:39,992 --> 00:17:42,161
I thought I was okay already.

257
00:17:45,623 --> 00:17:49,001
I thought I was returning
to my normal life.

258
00:17:53,631 --> 00:17:55,383
I thought I could handle it.

259
00:17:57,593 --> 00:17:59,554
Why is it like this?

260
00:18:07,645 --> 00:18:08,312
Ke.

261
00:18:09,605 --> 00:18:11,107
Healing is not linear.

262
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:16,654
It is normal to feel hurt and
to re-experience those emotions.

263
00:18:18,447 --> 00:18:21,200
That doesn’t mean you’ve
returned to square one.

264
00:18:22,410 --> 00:18:24,328
Progress is still progress.

265
00:18:26,706 --> 00:18:28,583
But when will I be
able to move forward?

266
00:18:32,810 --> 00:18:35,104
I don’t want to live
like this anymore, Sam.

267
00:18:36,799 --> 00:18:38,384
Sam, this is so hard.

268
00:18:39,093 --> 00:18:40,970
This is just so hard.

269
00:18:48,144 --> 00:18:52,857
Do you want to go back to therapy?
I have Dr. Peja’s number.

270
00:18:53,524 --> 00:18:56,110
It might help if you go back.

271
00:18:58,696 --> 00:18:59,614
Ke?

272
00:19:01,991 --> 00:19:04,493
Eat something first.
Do you still have a fever?

273
00:19:06,662 --> 00:19:09,624
You had a high fever a while ago. Thank
goodness it's already gone down for you.

274
00:19:09,713 --> 00:19:14,885
First, drink some water.
And here we have a salad for you to eat.

275
00:19:15,516 --> 00:19:18,352
Via, you got the wrong order.

276
00:19:18,377 --> 00:19:19,962
That is my order;
this one here is Kierra’s.

277
00:19:19,987 --> 00:19:20,702
Huh?

278
00:19:21,594 --> 00:19:22,220
Oh.

279
00:19:22,595 --> 00:19:24,055
How are you, dude?

280
00:19:25,431 --> 00:19:28,434
Sevi, you’re an idiot. I mean...

281
00:19:32,438 --> 00:19:34,106
See, now Ke’s stressed again.

282
00:19:34,273 --> 00:19:35,816
Because the other one’s my order.

283
00:19:35,816 --> 00:19:36,817
Don’t make a big deal out of it.

284
00:19:36,817 --> 00:19:38,527
Sevi, your order is incomplete.

285
00:19:39,070 --> 00:19:43,407
Can’t even do a simple task properly.
I’m so disappointed, bro.

286
00:19:44,450 --> 00:19:46,035
Hey, Ke. You’re awake now.

287
00:19:46,541 --> 00:19:49,293
You hardly ever show up, and when you do,
you make a lot of noise.

288
00:19:50,039 --> 00:19:50,790
Sorry.

289
00:19:51,332 --> 00:19:53,626
You’re so noisy!
Look what’s happened now.

290
00:19:53,834 --> 00:19:54,877
You’re disturbing Ke.

291
00:19:54,877 --> 00:19:56,170
Just go out first.

292
00:19:56,170 --> 00:19:57,588
- She said you guys should go out.
- Just go out.

293
00:19:57,588 --> 00:19:58,339
- All of you.
- Go out now.

294
00:19:58,339 --> 00:19:58,756
You go.

295
00:19:58,756 --> 00:20:00,633
No, don’t. Just eat here.

296
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:02,176
Don’t leave me.

297
00:20:19,478 --> 00:20:22,314
My ears are so used
to all your noise.

298
00:20:23,197 --> 00:20:24,365
Thank you, guys.

299
00:20:25,562 --> 00:20:26,939
Ah, that—

300
00:20:26,993 --> 00:20:28,411
Just hand over the food so she can eat.

301
00:20:28,411 --> 00:20:29,954
- No. Here, this is it, this one.
- Yeah, here, this one.

302
00:20:29,954 --> 00:20:31,455
- I just got my order.
- Just let her eat.

303
00:20:31,455 --> 00:20:32,999
This is yours. That’s yours, right?

304
00:20:33,624 --> 00:20:34,500
Here you go, Ke.

305
00:20:35,173 --> 00:20:37,169
This is the flavor you like, right?

306
00:20:38,296 --> 00:20:41,132
Okay, she’s going to eat now.

307
00:20:42,258 --> 00:20:43,467
Airplane.

308
00:20:45,011 --> 00:20:46,178
Baby.

309
00:20:46,178 --> 00:20:47,263
Who’s a little baby?

310
00:20:50,850 --> 00:20:51,767
Is it good?

311
00:20:54,603 --> 00:20:55,479
My turn.

312
00:20:55,896 --> 00:20:56,439
Why—

313
00:20:57,898 --> 00:20:58,816
Oh.

314
00:21:01,944 --> 00:21:05,281
What the hell! You like that huh?

315
00:21:05,281 --> 00:21:07,742
Such a flirt!

316
00:21:07,742 --> 00:21:09,035
You giddy now?

317
00:21:09,035 --> 00:21:09,827
Want some, bro?

318
00:21:10,202 --> 00:21:11,203
- I’ll pass.
- Your turn?

319
00:21:11,203 --> 00:21:12,163
Calories.

320
00:21:13,122 --> 00:21:14,999
Look at our baby.

321
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:12,550
I’m sorry for not finding
you fast enough. Still,

322
00:22:12,574 --> 00:22:16,546
you’llfeel safer with your friends’
touch. Get some rest.

323
00:22:24,443 --> 00:22:26,404
Hey! Shan!

324
00:22:27,084 --> 00:22:27,960
Miguel.

325
00:22:29,198 --> 00:22:30,741
Nice seeing you here.

326
00:22:42,802 --> 00:22:44,275
Ciandrei, sorry if...

327
00:22:49,578 --> 00:22:50,698
Hi Ciandrei.

328
00:22:55,868 --> 00:22:57,374
Hi, Kierra. How are you?

329
00:23:01,926 --> 00:23:03,660
Are you okay?

330
00:23:11,269 --> 00:23:12,979
I’m going to buy a coffee.
Do you want anything?

331
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:16,078
No. I’m going to buy some turon outside,
so I’ll come back for you.

332
00:23:16,245 --> 00:23:16,971
What else?

333
00:23:16,996 --> 00:23:17,580
This too.

334
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:19,415
Okay, okay. Thank you, thank you.

335
00:23:19,473 --> 00:23:20,432
Do you want some crackers?

336
00:23:20,971 --> 00:23:22,055
- How about this one?
- Excuse me.

337
00:23:22,657 --> 00:23:23,575
Excuse me, please.

338
00:23:23,808 --> 00:23:25,059
Sorry. Excuse me.

339
00:23:25,796 --> 00:23:26,464
Look over there.

340
00:23:26,464 --> 00:23:27,047
Hey.

341
00:23:27,430 --> 00:23:28,681
Sorry. Excuse me.

342
00:23:29,425 --> 00:23:30,384
Excuse me.

343
00:23:59,622 --> 00:24:00,415
What?

344
00:24:03,334 --> 00:24:04,251
Are you okay?

345
00:24:04,971 --> 00:24:06,306
I’m sorry.

346
00:24:07,296 --> 00:24:08,172
Ke…

347
00:24:08,923 --> 00:24:10,424
- Hey. Breathe, breathe, breathe.
- I’m sorry, Luna.

348
00:24:10,758 --> 00:24:11,133
No.

349
00:24:11,133 --> 00:24:12,676
I’m sorry, I’m still like this.

350
00:24:13,177 --> 00:24:15,596
No. You don’t need to apologize, it’s okay.

351
00:24:16,222 --> 00:24:17,264
You’re okay.

352
00:24:18,390 --> 00:24:19,600
Okay? Breathe.

353
00:24:22,311 --> 00:24:23,604
Let’s go. Come on.

354
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:34,990
Let’s go to BGC later.

355
00:24:34,990 --> 00:24:37,409
- It’s the weekend anyway.
- Hey! Sure, let’s go.

356
00:24:37,409 --> 00:24:39,703
Luna, Ke. Message Via, too.

357
00:24:39,703 --> 00:24:43,666
Oh, Via is in Katip for a reason.
As for me, I don’t want to go.

358
00:24:43,666 --> 00:24:46,168
I don’t want to study at the last minute.
I have so many projects to do.

359
00:24:46,168 --> 00:24:49,547
And I still have many
plates to finish, so no.

360
00:24:49,547 --> 00:24:50,923
What about you, Ke? Let’s go.

361
00:24:50,923 --> 00:24:51,507
Huh?

362
00:24:51,507 --> 00:24:53,259
Uh, I can’t make it.

363
00:24:54,093 --> 00:24:55,052
That’s lame.

364
00:24:55,052 --> 00:24:57,263
You always used to join us before.

365
00:24:57,263 --> 00:25:00,683
Come on. Leave Ke alone;
she still has a lot to do. She’s busy, too.

366
00:25:00,683 --> 00:25:01,725
We’ll make it up to you next time.

367
00:25:01,725 --> 00:25:02,351
Okay, then.

368
00:25:02,351 --> 00:25:02,893
Mhmm.

369
00:25:02,893 --> 00:25:03,852
Ah, I know.

370
00:25:04,103 --> 00:25:05,521
Let’s just invite Jann instead.

371
00:25:05,521 --> 00:25:06,146
- Right.
- Let’s go.

372
00:25:06,146 --> 00:25:06,981
Come on. Let’s go!

373
00:25:06,981 --> 00:25:07,731
That’s right.

374
00:25:10,317 --> 00:25:10,943
Ke.

375
00:25:11,822 --> 00:25:13,574
My meeting might run late tonight.

376
00:25:14,280 --> 00:25:16,699
Do you want me to call Sam so
you have someone to go home with?

377
00:25:16,907 --> 00:25:18,284
No, it’s okay, Luna.

378
00:25:18,284 --> 00:25:20,369
Let’s not bother Sam.
It’ll just be a hassle.

379
00:25:20,536 --> 00:25:22,496
I’ll just wait for you. I’m fine with that.

380
00:25:22,663 --> 00:25:23,080
Sure?

381
00:25:23,080 --> 00:25:23,497
Mhmm.

382
00:25:23,497 --> 00:25:24,123
Okay.

383
00:25:24,707 --> 00:25:25,541
Okay!

384
00:25:28,627 --> 00:25:29,398
Ke!

385
00:25:31,088 --> 00:25:31,962
- Hey.
- Are you hungry?

386
00:25:32,860 --> 00:25:33,701
Do you want some?

387
00:25:34,936 --> 00:25:35,898
Is this a scam?

388
00:25:36,468 --> 00:25:40,055
This looks like a scam.
Suddenly, you’ll make me pay for this.

389
00:25:40,414 --> 00:25:41,373
Where did you get this anyway?

390
00:25:41,932 --> 00:25:45,936
Relax. I just bought it from some
high school seniors who were selling it.

391
00:25:51,817 --> 00:25:54,903
What are you doing here all alone?
Are you waiting for someone?

392
00:25:55,654 --> 00:25:57,781
I am waiting for Luna
to finish her meeting.

393
00:25:58,741 --> 00:26:00,284
I’m already sleepy, though.

394
00:26:03,203 --> 00:26:06,957
I also have a meeting later,
but I’ll keep you company for now.

395
00:26:07,333 --> 00:26:08,334
Won’t you be late?

396
00:26:09,585 --> 00:26:10,961
No. It’s fine.

397
00:26:14,590 --> 00:26:17,343
Wow. You’re very sleepy.

398
00:26:18,427 --> 00:26:19,428
Haven't you slept at all?

399
00:26:20,095 --> 00:26:21,972
I stayed up all night reviewing.

400
00:26:28,145 --> 00:26:31,440
You can lean on me.
Take a nap.

401
00:26:31,899 --> 00:26:32,650
You sure?

402
00:26:33,150 --> 00:26:33,942
Yeah.

403
00:26:58,300 --> 00:26:59,343
Hey.

404
00:27:01,345 --> 00:27:04,807
Oh no, I’m sorry. You still have
your meeting, and you’re already late.

405
00:27:04,807 --> 00:27:07,559
No, it’s no problem.
In any case, the meeting didn’t take place.

406
00:27:07,559 --> 00:27:08,936
It didn’t push through?

407
00:27:08,936 --> 00:27:11,480
How would that work,
if you are the leader and are not present?

408
00:27:11,730 --> 00:27:12,690
You really are a dumbass.

409
00:27:12,690 --> 00:27:14,483
You should have woken me up.

410
00:27:14,483 --> 00:27:17,569
You know what?
Don’t pay any attention to Sevi, okay?

411
00:27:17,979 --> 00:27:19,897
The meeting wasn’t even that important.

412
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:22,239
I’m sorry, Ke. We’re late.

413
00:27:22,264 --> 00:27:23,974
Do you want to have dinner? Let’s go.

414
00:27:23,999 --> 00:27:25,027
Sure, that works.

415
00:27:25,630 --> 00:27:27,006
Okay. Theo and I are going too.

416
00:27:27,031 --> 00:27:29,241
You’re treating us,
since you ditched us up at the meeting.

417
00:27:29,289 --> 00:27:30,749
- He’s treating us to everything.
- Right, right.

418
00:27:30,749 --> 00:27:31,375
Just order whatever you want.

419
00:27:31,375 --> 00:27:32,292
Nice.

420
00:27:33,961 --> 00:27:34,628
Fine.

421
00:27:34,628 --> 00:27:35,129
My treat.

422
00:27:35,129 --> 00:27:38,549
Yes! Free dinner!

423
00:27:38,549 --> 00:27:40,509
- So dramatic.
- Come on, let’s go. I’m hungry already.

424
00:27:40,509 --> 00:27:41,385
Let’s go.

425
00:27:43,512 --> 00:27:48,142
Class, in the case of The
Republic v. Sandiganbayan—

426
00:27:48,851 --> 00:27:51,395
were the private respondents correct

427
00:27:51,395 --> 00:27:56,191
in questioning the legality of
the search and seizure of their properties—

428
00:27:56,191 --> 00:27:58,703
even if there was a search warrant?

429
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,180
What can you say, Mr. Lopez?

430
00:28:09,580 --> 00:28:13,125
Yes, Attorney. The search warrant
was only for firearms and ammunition—

431
00:28:13,125 --> 00:28:17,129
hence, the PCGG seized items
that aren’t included in the search warrant.

432
00:28:17,189 --> 00:28:19,816
But it happened during
the interregnum period.

433
00:28:20,143 --> 00:28:23,526
Could they validly
invoke their rights against

434
00:28:23,550 --> 00:28:26,858
unlawful search and
seizure, Mr. Villaflor?

435
00:28:27,791 --> 00:28:28,459
No.

436
00:28:29,765 --> 00:28:32,575
No, they cannot. During
the interregnum period,

437
00:28:32,599 --> 00:28:35,103
the 1973 constitution
was not in effect.

438
00:28:35,230 --> 00:28:39,902
Therefore, the private respondents
did not enjoy any constitutional rights.

439
00:28:40,235 --> 00:28:41,695
Do you agree, Mr. Lopez?

440
00:28:42,654 --> 00:28:43,363
No.

441
00:28:43,906 --> 00:28:44,907
Not at all.

442
00:28:45,199 --> 00:28:48,827
It is correct that the Bill of Rights
of the 1973 constitution was not in effect,

443
00:28:48,827 --> 00:28:52,498
but the revolutionary government
was still obligated under international law

444
00:28:52,498 --> 00:28:55,542
to observe the rights of
the private respondents.

445
00:28:55,542 --> 00:28:57,536
The Philippines
was a signatory of the

446
00:28:57,560 --> 00:29:00,422
International Covenant
on Civil and Political Rights

447
00:29:00,422 --> 00:29:02,549
and even Universal
Declaration of Human Rights.

448
00:29:02,674 --> 00:29:03,675
So, no.

449
00:29:05,093 --> 00:29:08,514
Even in extreme,
extraordinary situations...

450
00:29:09,306 --> 00:29:10,534
No one is above the law.

451
00:29:26,740 --> 00:29:28,033
Lopez.

452
00:29:28,617 --> 00:29:29,493
What’s up?

453
00:29:31,662 --> 00:29:32,746
What now?

454
00:29:34,581 --> 00:29:35,249
What?

455
00:29:35,707 --> 00:29:38,001
You wanna see my dick
and compare sizes or what?

456
00:29:38,627 --> 00:29:40,671
What? Yo, chill.

457
00:29:41,463 --> 00:29:42,339
Chill.

458
00:29:42,339 --> 00:29:44,967
Take it easy, man.
Why are you so pissed off at me?

459
00:29:45,592 --> 00:29:48,178
What’s up? Did I do something to you?

460
00:29:48,399 --> 00:29:51,527
Or are you perhaps threatened?

461
00:29:51,974 --> 00:29:54,726
Because our professors always
have us arguing against each other?

462
00:29:54,726 --> 00:29:55,769
‘Cause I understand.

463
00:29:56,228 --> 00:29:57,145
I understand.

464
00:29:57,302 --> 00:30:01,264
Bro, come on.
You don’t even know the title of the case.

465
00:30:01,289 --> 00:30:02,707
Why would I be threatened by you?

466
00:30:03,068 --> 00:30:05,821
Why would I be threatened
by an idiot like you?

467
00:30:09,136 --> 00:30:09,928
Dude.

468
00:30:11,910 --> 00:30:12,703
Bro.

469
00:30:12,804 --> 00:30:13,513
Come on.

470
00:30:14,329 --> 00:30:15,956
I’ve been nice to you, right?

471
00:30:16,465 --> 00:30:17,549
Be nice to me.

472
00:30:18,458 --> 00:30:19,334
Right?

473
00:30:20,127 --> 00:30:21,378
Do you know Kierra?

474
00:30:29,720 --> 00:30:32,347
Why would you mention
a random girl’s name?

475
00:30:35,976 --> 00:30:37,144
Open the door, will you?

476
00:30:37,978 --> 00:30:40,480
It stinks in here. Let’s go.

477
00:30:54,077 --> 00:30:56,538
When was the last time you had a nightmare?

478
00:30:58,040 --> 00:30:59,235
Yesterday.

479
00:31:00,876 --> 00:31:01,819
I see.

480
00:31:03,339 --> 00:31:04,632
Hold on to this.

481
00:31:05,297 --> 00:31:06,381
This should help.

482
00:31:10,636 --> 00:31:14,556
So, you’re dreaming of the same scenario?

483
00:31:16,683 --> 00:31:20,604
No, it’s like a puzzle.

484
00:31:22,147 --> 00:31:32,157
It’s a different setting,
but it’s always about that night.

485
00:31:34,701 --> 00:31:39,831
It’s always about how he hurt me.

486
00:31:43,335 --> 00:31:45,253
Which night are you pertaining to?

487
00:31:51,385 --> 00:31:52,594
The...

488
00:31:54,221 --> 00:31:57,057
The night I got hospitalized.

489
00:32:05,772 --> 00:32:07,734
I’m sorry, I want to go home.

490
00:32:08,527 --> 00:32:09,611
I’m sorry.

491
00:32:09,611 --> 00:32:11,071
No, it’s okay.

492
00:32:11,321 --> 00:32:13,115
You don’t have to say sorry, Kierra.

493
00:32:14,658 --> 00:32:16,743
We’ll take it slow, okay?

494
00:32:18,829 --> 00:32:19,997
Baby steps.

495
00:32:41,184 --> 00:32:42,644
Hey, Ke!

496
00:32:42,811 --> 00:32:43,687
Theo!

497
00:32:43,832 --> 00:32:46,793
You’re here, too. Seems like
this is your favorite spot now, huh?

498
00:32:46,940 --> 00:32:49,818
Yeah. Actually, I prefer studying here.

499
00:32:50,216 --> 00:32:51,926
Are you going to study,
too? Let’s just share a table.

500
00:32:52,529 --> 00:32:54,031
Why are you alone?

501
00:32:56,241 --> 00:32:57,242
Don’t you have a date?

502
00:32:57,909 --> 00:32:58,660
A date?

503
00:32:59,411 --> 00:33:00,412
Should I have one?

504
00:33:01,621 --> 00:33:04,416
Sorry. I’m sorry, guys.
I didn’t know.

505
00:33:04,791 --> 00:33:05,709
It’s just me.

506
00:33:06,835 --> 00:33:10,797
Poor thing. Well,
I’ll be your date tonight.

507
00:33:14,968 --> 00:33:16,011
Just for tonight?

508
00:33:17,262 --> 00:33:19,347
Do you want me
to be your date every day?

509
00:33:19,806 --> 00:33:23,060
Win me over first.
I’m not that easy.

510
00:33:25,645 --> 00:33:26,855
If that’s the case—

511
00:33:28,857 --> 00:33:30,275
can I court you?

512
00:33:32,986 --> 00:33:35,072
Quit messing around. I’ll order first.

513
00:33:35,072 --> 00:33:36,031
Want some cake?

514
00:33:37,866 --> 00:33:38,992
Yeah, sure.

515
00:33:38,992 --> 00:33:39,993
Okay.

516
00:33:45,499 --> 00:33:46,249
Hi.

517
00:33:46,274 --> 00:33:48,318
Hi, what are you getting?

518
00:33:48,752 --> 00:33:51,421
Two oreo cheesecakes and—

519
00:33:51,421 --> 00:33:55,133
What do you have today?
Is the Sakura drink available?

520
00:33:56,635 --> 00:33:57,594
For you or for him?

521
00:33:58,294 --> 00:33:59,045
For him?

522
00:33:59,257 --> 00:34:00,050
Unavailable.

523
00:34:00,097 --> 00:34:00,806
For me.

524
00:34:00,806 --> 00:34:01,973
Still unavailable.

525
00:34:02,516 --> 00:34:03,767
Okay.

526
00:34:04,267 --> 00:34:05,936
One iced Americano.

527
00:34:06,853 --> 00:34:11,650
Alright, so, two Oreo cheesecakes
and an iced Americano. 600.

528
00:34:15,695 --> 00:34:16,363
Thank you.

529
00:34:16,388 --> 00:34:18,431
I will call you by your name
when your order is ready.

530
00:34:19,241 --> 00:34:20,024
Okay.

531
00:34:54,359 --> 00:34:55,569
She’s going to melt.

532
00:34:56,695 --> 00:34:57,779
What was that, sir?

533
00:35:00,282 --> 00:35:04,828
I said, can you check the temperature
of our fridge? The cakes might melt.

534
00:35:04,828 --> 00:35:06,204
- Sure thing, sir.
- Thank you.

535
00:35:18,049 --> 00:35:18,884
Oh my god.

536
00:35:19,009 --> 00:35:19,885
Shit!

537
00:35:19,885 --> 00:35:20,844
Sorry, sorry. Did I get you wet?

538
00:35:20,844 --> 00:35:22,387
No, no. But I have tissues.

539
00:35:22,721 --> 00:35:25,432
Alex, can you help them
with their table, please? Thanks.

540
00:35:25,973 --> 00:35:27,654
- Shit. This is so embarrassing.
- I’ll take care of it.

541
00:35:27,679 --> 00:35:29,154
Can I even come back here?

542
00:35:29,622 --> 00:35:30,248
Ow!

543
00:35:30,520 --> 00:35:31,438
Uh, sure—

544
00:35:31,563 --> 00:35:32,397
Are you okay?

545
00:35:32,397 --> 00:35:33,231
No, I’m fine.

546
00:35:34,065 --> 00:35:35,108
Do you need ice or anything?

547
00:35:35,108 --> 00:35:35,901
No, no.

548
00:35:35,901 --> 00:35:36,610
I’m fine.

549
00:35:36,610 --> 00:35:37,444
Shit.

550
00:35:39,279 --> 00:35:39,988
I’m sorry, sir.

551
00:35:39,988 --> 00:35:40,947
It’s okay.

552
00:35:53,210 --> 00:35:54,211
Sure, you’re okay?

553
00:35:54,211 --> 00:35:55,212
Mhmm.

554
00:36:21,696 --> 00:36:24,449
Hey, what’s up? Where were you?

555
00:36:24,449 --> 00:36:26,993
The cafe. It’s close by, so...

556
00:36:26,993 --> 00:36:28,036
Ah…

557
00:36:33,833 --> 00:36:34,960
Did you go see him?

558
00:36:35,252 --> 00:36:37,462
Nope. I studied.

559
00:36:37,462 --> 00:36:38,630
Ah…

560
00:36:40,257 --> 00:36:41,424
But was he there?

561
00:36:44,970 --> 00:36:46,388
You two still aren’t talking?

562
00:36:51,726 --> 00:36:55,563
You know, they say
that when you like someone,

563
00:36:56,273 --> 00:36:57,816
you can’t stand being
away from that person.

564
00:36:59,234 --> 00:37:02,112
He never said that he liked me.

565
00:37:03,613 --> 00:37:05,448
I’m the only one who feels this way.

566
00:37:06,408 --> 00:37:08,952
Maybe I’m the problem.

567
00:37:10,704 --> 00:37:11,538
Ke.

568
00:37:12,747 --> 00:37:14,958
You’re not the problem, okay?

569
00:37:15,625 --> 00:37:18,295
Maybe he’s just being careful.

570
00:37:18,670 --> 00:37:21,089
Especially after what happened last time.

571
00:37:23,216 --> 00:37:24,968
Does he know about—

572
00:37:25,802 --> 00:37:26,845
No.

573
00:37:27,470 --> 00:37:29,139
I haven’t told him yet.

574
00:37:29,806 --> 00:37:33,184
And now I wonder if
they are really friends.

575
00:37:33,768 --> 00:37:35,979
Does he even know
what kind of person he is?

576
00:37:37,272 --> 00:37:39,649
I mean, are you sure they’re friends?

577
00:37:42,736 --> 00:37:48,158
If I were you, I would talk to him
so that you stop thinking about it.

578
00:37:49,075 --> 00:37:54,289
I think you’ve reached the point
where you can no longer ignore him.

579
00:37:56,583 --> 00:37:59,836
Once and for all.
Clear things up with him.

580
00:38:16,811 --> 00:38:18,229
Hi, Miss Kierra.

581
00:38:30,492 --> 00:38:32,994
Hello, is there anything you want?

582
00:38:32,994 --> 00:38:34,204
What’s your order for today, ma’am?

583
00:38:34,204 --> 00:38:35,413
Sakura drink.

584
00:38:35,622 --> 00:38:36,581
Okay.

585
00:38:39,125 --> 00:38:40,418
Do you like anything else?

586
00:38:50,720 --> 00:38:51,554
Ke.

587
00:38:53,139 --> 00:38:54,891
Stop caring, please.

588
00:38:59,938 --> 00:39:01,856
You know it’s not good for you.

589
00:39:48,027 --> 00:39:50,113
Do you have iced honey lemonade here?

590
00:39:52,615 --> 00:39:54,117
It’s not on the menu.

591
00:39:59,789 --> 00:40:01,082
Even for Acel?

592
00:40:04,836 --> 00:40:06,212
Okay fine, I’ll make one.

593
00:40:07,046 --> 00:40:09,424
Don’t make it too sweet, okay?
Acel doesn’t like things sweet.

594
00:40:10,049 --> 00:40:10,800
It’s not—

595
00:40:10,800 --> 00:40:11,551
I mean, it’s fine.

596
00:40:11,551 --> 00:40:13,595
Come on, it’s embarrassing—
it’s not on the menu.

597
00:40:13,595 --> 00:40:15,013
Don’t worry about it, Acel.

598
00:40:15,038 --> 00:40:18,041
Shan is more than willing to
make us any drink we want.

599
00:40:28,109 --> 00:40:29,736
Why do you look so down?

600
00:40:31,404 --> 00:40:32,197
Huh?

601
00:40:33,072 --> 00:40:34,324
No, I’m not.

602
00:40:35,366 --> 00:40:37,118
She hasn’t contacted you yet, huh?

603
00:40:37,827 --> 00:40:39,704
Wait, who’s “she”?

604
00:40:40,121 --> 00:40:44,125
Is this the girl they say
you’re taking seriously?

605
00:40:52,300 --> 00:40:53,635
What did you tell him?

606
00:40:54,302 --> 00:40:55,803
Nothing.

607
00:40:56,221 --> 00:40:57,096
Let’s order.

608
00:40:59,140 --> 00:41:00,225
Seriously, Haze.

609
00:41:00,934 --> 00:41:02,936
It’s no surprise that
people say you’re a gossip.

610
00:41:03,061 --> 00:41:05,104
Why? Who texted me?

611
00:41:08,983 --> 00:41:11,778
What’s going on?
Hasn’t she contacted you yet?

612
00:41:12,305 --> 00:41:14,072
I’m still giving her space.

613
00:41:15,156 --> 00:41:17,492
- I’m not reaching out to her either.
- Space?

614
00:41:17,492 --> 00:41:20,745
What if she’s also
waiting for you to reach out?

615
00:41:20,870 --> 00:41:25,959
Look, Shan, just talk to her already.
Don’t let her beat you to it.

616
00:41:33,383 --> 00:41:36,594
I didn’t know you could be this shy.

617
00:41:41,849 --> 00:41:47,814
You know what? If you’re just going to
provoke me, then order for more—alright?

618
00:41:47,814 --> 00:41:50,733
Fine, I’ll make your iced honey lemonade.

619
00:41:50,733 --> 00:41:52,151
Thank you.

620
00:41:54,704 --> 00:41:55,788
Make it two!

621
00:41:56,988 --> 00:41:58,906
Welcome to Valeria High!

622
00:41:59,748 --> 00:42:01,542
We do the events here sometimes.

623
00:42:01,828 --> 00:42:04,038
Actually, no, there are
a bunch of booths here.

624
00:42:04,414 --> 00:42:05,665
How do you know that?

625
00:42:05,665 --> 00:42:06,958
Wait, where did you
go to high school again?

626
00:42:07,417 --> 00:42:08,376
Lopez High.

627
00:42:08,376 --> 00:42:11,838
Let’s start making your yesterdays happy—
starting today.

628
00:42:12,886 --> 00:42:15,108
Is there something that’s making you happy?

629
00:42:15,133 --> 00:42:16,593
Or is it someone?

630
00:42:16,593 --> 00:42:17,677
Or is it someone?

631
00:42:17,677 --> 00:42:18,511
Good night.

632
00:42:18,511 --> 00:42:19,304
Good night.

633
00:42:19,304 --> 00:42:20,930
And see you yesterday.

634
00:42:21,222 --> 00:42:22,849
I just wanna know something, bro.

635
00:42:22,849 --> 00:42:23,808
You mentioned Kierra.

636
00:42:24,100 --> 00:42:24,892
Why?

637
00:42:25,351 --> 00:42:27,061
Is she still crazy?

638
00:42:27,061 --> 00:42:27,812
Shut up.

639
00:42:27,812 --> 00:42:33,484
He was just really manipulative.

640
00:42:33,484 --> 00:42:36,404
You believe me, right?
I wouldn’t lie to you.

641
00:42:36,404 --> 00:42:38,281
Let it go. It’s nothing. I promise you.

642
00:42:38,281 --> 00:42:38,781
Let it go.

643
00:42:38,781 --> 00:42:41,909
And he cheated on me, too.

644
00:42:41,909 --> 00:42:43,453
I fucking told you that.

645
00:42:44,245 --> 00:42:46,998
You did not betray yourself, Kierra.

646
00:42:48,249 --> 00:42:49,542
He betrayed you.

647
00:42:49,542 --> 00:42:51,252
She almost ruined my life.

648
00:42:51,419 --> 00:42:53,838
- Bro, she’s got some screws—
- I said shut up!
